summary:
FAIL, with one new Medium finding (D-192: a Medium must be repaired before the gate) and one new Low.
- Both open findings verify CLOSED_VERIFIED on candidate d62b187b: F-DG6-920 (the round-1 probe now fails as intended; context-recheck passes 67/67; a mutant ignoring context_records is caught) and F-DG6-900 (the demo-stack probe shows 'Comparison basis: Baseline and formula version validated by Finance' in en and ar; a mutant restoring the old labels is caught).
- F-DG6-970 (Medium, REQ-S17-007): after a revocation, the now-withheld earlier answer is still sent to the model as conversation history (conversations.ts:440-449 historyOf). Its text comes back in a new answer served with contentWithheld false and context_records []. Reproduced with the shipped http_endpoint provider and a loopback echo model.
- F-DG6-971 (Low): the NOT VALID CHECK assistant_suggestion_context_records_required is still enforced on UPDATE, so a pre-0128 suggestion can never be taken to a draft (422), contrary to the documented fallback.
Everything else passes on this candidate:
- candidate ID verified four ways; build, typecheck, lint, format, openapi-lint (932) and no-cdn;
- pnpm test on Node 22 (exit 0) and Node 24 (every test passes; exit 1 is a Vitest worker RPC timeout under load, cleared by a --maxWorkers=2 re-run);
- integration in both locales: 440 files, 4360 passed, 1 skip by design, 1 stale todo, contract 932/932;
- e2e in en and ar: 42 tests, with a loopback-only A21 connection log;
- validators DG5-DG1 historical and the DG6 register;
- the AUD/ADM-only sweep, the token probes and the F-DG6-380 probe;
- log and secret scans.
The D-228 (4)/D-229 open questions are judged acceptable. Disclosures: an ENOSPC on the shared volume forced a lean --shared, sparse clone; Node 22 is v22.22.0; my own legacy probe needed three runs to set up its pre-0128 state; HEAD moved to the domain reviewer's auto-commit, whose files I did not open.
